<title>UK: S.Electric see 165 mln stg windfall tax hit.</title>
<headline>S.Electric see 165 mln stg windfall tax hit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's last remaining independent regional electricity company (Rec) Southern Electric Plc said on Wednesday it expected its share of a utility tax announced by the government to be around 165 million stg.</p>
<p>&quot;Based on our interpretation of the (budget) statement, our provisional estimates are around 165 million stg,&quot; a spokesman said.</p>
</text>
